## THE MOVE RULE AND ITS APPLICATION (a reading, stated)
`NexusAI/CLAUDE.md:299-303` ("When completing work"): `:302` "Code change -> `Testing`", `:303` "Decision / docs / non-code -> straight to `Done`". **Reading, for RD-919:** its Done-when has two limbs joined by "or". The first limb is met on both halves: the written assessment exists (203 lines, 6 measured candidates, a recommendation at `:170`), and the product owner "has chosen ... to stay on sqlite3 6" and named node:sqlite (the ruling above). The ticket says "This ticket builds and changes nothing", so it is a decision ticket: by `:303` it goes straight to **Done**, not Testing (`:302` is for a code change) and not Release Ready. The second limb ("closed with the decision recorded") is also satisfied once the C-230 entry and the comment exist, so the move comes AFTER both are read back. Two things the reading does not hide: (1) the ticket's purpose, "before a fix is needed", is carried after closing by the four triggers in the entry and the comment, not by an open ticket; whether a standing watch ticket is wanted is Tuesday's question (default: no, the product owner asked only for the triggers to be recorded). (2) Done is the seat's act only under slot `MOVE919`; the default is `DONE`. **RD-918 does not move** (its two parts are open: the approve entry and the compose path). The seat may set exactly these states: **RD-919 To Do to Done (id 41 by name Done, under Job E's predicate)**; every ticket it creates stays at its creation state To Do; id 51 (Declined), 31 and 101 are never used; RD-918, RD-494, RD-913 and every other key are untouched.

