- `<W4-BLUF>` = docker/docker-compose.yml names three Dockerfiles: docker/Dockerfile.frontend (line 8), docker/Dockerfile.backend (line 23) and docker/Dockerfile.codellama (line 45). Only docker/Dockerfile.backend is tracked, and RD-494 holds that it cannot build because its line 8 copies backend/package*.json, which matches nothing. The other two files do not exist in the repository, so a compose build fails for the frontend and codellama services as well, before any driver question arises. The successor assessment of 2026-11-02 found this while checking part (b) of RD-918. Nothing in the customer image uses this path; RD-494 records that it is not part of the customer image or any registry build.
