- `<C230-HEAD>` = **C-230. THE PRODUCT OWNER'S RULING (2026-11-02 10:30:12 AEDT, live board): NexusAI stays on sqlite3 6.0.1 for now and names node:sqlite, the driver built into Node, as its successor; nothing is built (RD-919).**
- `<C230-VERB>` = **Verbatim.** The ruling was a choice of an option: "a <EMDASH> Stay on sqlite3 and name node:sqlite as successor (recommended)", with the option's own detail "The next NexusAI records seat records the four triggers for reassessing: an unfixed advisory, node:sqlite reaching stable, npm blocking install scripts by default, or a Node release the driver cannot load on. Nothing is built." Source: the live board, the answer to the question on RD-919 (options: (a) the one chosen, (b) "Start the preparation only", (c) "Move to node:sqlite now"); the decision store holds the choice at 10:30:49 AEDT. The decision's own identifier is not copied here.
- `<C230-SETTLES>` = **What it settles.** (1) NexusAI stays on sqlite3 6.0.1: no package, lock, image, code or configuration change follows from this ruling. (2) node:sqlite is the named successor; no other candidate is chosen. (3) The four triggers are the standing conditions for reassessing, in the wording of the successor assessment (Briefs/2026-11-02_B1100_SQLITE3-SUCCESSOR-ASSESSMENT.md, sha256 9441b0e719e9dc0812f1af5b64aba7bb0de68e63bb4fc41ed50b05dd4363a256, section "What would change it"): (a) an advisory against sqlite3 6.0.1, its production install chain, or SQLite 3.52.0 as bundled, with no upstream fix; (b) node:sqlite reaching Stability 2 on the Node line the image uses (read the line in the Node docs for that line; today 24.x prints 1.2); (c) npm enabling default-deny for install scripts without a simple approve entry, or the image build ceasing to be able to reach GitHub release assets; (d) a Node major that changes N-API behaviour so the napi-v6 binding stops loading. If (b) alone fires, moving is optional rather than urgent. (4) RD-919's done-when is met by that assessment and this ruling.
- `<C230-NOT>` = **What it does not settle.** (1) Options (b) and (c) were not chosen: the preparation (the 5 double-quoted SQL literals, the raw database calls routed through one module, the install-script approve entry) and the move to node:sqlite are not authorised and would need a new ruling. (2) Whether a release-candidate built-in is acceptable for the data store, and on which Node line: asked only if a trigger fires. (3) RD-918 (the install-script entry and the compose path) is not ruled here. (4) The latent defects the assessment found on the way are not ruled; the tickets filed for them are named in the HISTORY entry of this record. (5) The option's detail says "a Node release the driver cannot load on" and the assessment says "a Node major that changes N-API behaviour so the napi-v6 binding stops loading": this entry keeps both and treats the assessment's wording as the operative test. (6) The hold of [[C-224]] (no NexusAI demo deploy until RD-876 part 2 lands) is unchanged.
- `<C230-REL>` = Related: RD-919, RD-918, RD-913, RD-494, [[C-229]], [[C-224]], [[C-190]]. Recorded by the B1114 seat (R133), 2026-11-02.

